# ◈ packages.calamares.list — installer stack
#
# ASSUMPTION (flag if wrong): Qt5 + KDE Frameworks 5, not Qt6/KF6. Rationale —
# Qt5/KF5 has a longer track record building under musl (other musl distros'
# Calamares packaging is still mostly Qt5-based); Qt6/KF6 musl support is
# newer and less proven. Worth revisiting once KF6 musl builds are more
# battle-tested elsewhere.
#
# OPEN ITEM: Calamares + KPMcore may not live in the main Gentoo tree in
# every version — check whether your Catalyst portage confdir already has
# an overlay enabled (e.g. GURU) before this builds. If not, build-packages.yml
# will need an `eselect repository enable guru && emaint sync --repo guru`
# step (or equivalent) added ahead of the emerge step for this list. Flagging
# rather than assuming, since I haven't verified current package.mask state
# for your exact profile.
#
# qtwayland is included on the assumption the graphics stack is Wayland+cage
# (see packages.graphics.list) — Calamares needs it to run as a native
# Wayland client rather than falling back to XWayland.

dev-qt/qtcore
dev-qt/qtgui
dev-qt/qtwidgets
dev-qt/qtnetwork
dev-qt/qtsvg
dev-qt/qtdeclarative
dev-qt/qtquickcontrols2
dev-qt/qtwayland
dev-qt/qttranslations
dev-qt/qtdbus

kde-frameworks/extra-cmake-modules
kde-frameworks/kcoreaddons
kde-frameworks/kconfig
kde-frameworks/kconfigwidgets
kde-frameworks/kwidgetsaddons
kde-frameworks/kiconthemes
kde-frameworks/ki18n
kde-frameworks/solid
kde-frameworks/kservice
kde-frameworks/kpackage

sys-libs/kpmcore
sys-block/parted
sys-fs/lvm2
sys-fs/cryptsetup
sys-fs/e2fsprogs
sys-fs/dosfstools
sys-fs/ntfs3g

app-crypt/polkit
dev-libs/yaml-cpp
dev-libs/boost

app-admin/calamares               use:-qml,qt5
